      <data key="d12">DHRS2</data>
      <data key="d13">Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 2, mitochondrial; Displays NADPH-dependent dicarbonyl reductase activity in vitro with 3,4-Hexanedione, 2,3-Heptanedione and 1-Phenyl-1,2- propanedione as substrates. No reductase activity is displayed in vitro with steroids, retinoids and sugars as substrates. Attenuates MDM2- mediated p53/TP53 degradation, leading to p53/TP53 stabilization and increased transcription activity, resulting in the accumulation of MDM2 and CDKN1A/p21; Belongs to the short-chain dehydrogenases/reductases (SDR) family.</data>
      <data key="d14">Q13268</data>
      <data key="d15">Q13268</data>
